<title>USA: Uruguay files with U.S. SEC for $300 mln in bonds.</title>
<headline>Uruguay files with U.S. SEC for $300 mln in bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Republic of Uruguay filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a registration to sell up to $300 million in bonds due 2027.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through ING Barings.</p>
<p>Net proceeds from the bonds will be used to refinance debt to achieve a longer maturity profile and to finance the general activities of the government.</p>
</text>
